1
00:00:17,120 --> 00:00:24,460
We sigh whenever we're about to come to a standstill

2
00:00:17,120 --> 00:00:24,460
Owarinaki tabi no tochuu tachidomarisouna toki

3
00:00:24,460 --> 00:00:30,710
While moving on this endless journey.

4
00:00:24,460 --> 00:00:30,710
Fukai tameiki kobosu bokura wa

5
00:00:32,800 --> 00:00:38,430
Everytime we lunge for it, it escapes and flies off.

6
00:00:32,800 --> 00:00:38,430
Tsukamikaketewa mata hanareteitta

7
00:00:38,890 --> 00:00:45,850
But now, there's nothing to be afraid of

8
00:00:38,890 --> 00:00:45,850
Demo ima wa mou nanimo osoreru koto wa nai

9
00:00:46,480 --> 00:00:53,780
The powerful ties that bind our hearts

10
00:00:46,480 --> 00:00:53,780
Kokoro wo tsunagu tsuyoi kizuna wa

11
00:00:53,780 --> 00:00:59,240
Will never come loose.

12
00:00:53,780 --> 00:00:59,240
Keshite hodoke wa shinai sa

13
00:01:01,280 --> 00:01:08,960
After a lifetime of searching, we finally arrived

14
00:01:01,280 --> 00:01:08,960
Sagashitsuzukete tadoritsuita

15
00:01:08,960 --> 00:01:14,760
Here, where the period lies.

16
00:01:08,960 --> 00:01:14,760
Kono basho de piriodo ni

17
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:24,060
Let's change all our sorrow and rage to power.

18
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:24,060
Kanashimi ikari chikara ni kaete

19
00:01:24,060 --> 00:01:28,980
Destiny is right within our reach.

20
00:01:24,060 --> 00:01:28,980
Unmei wa sugu soba ni

21
00:01:35,530 --> 00:01:39,860
So you're suggesting Major General Armstrong had a hand in Lieutenant General Raven's disappearance?

22
00:01:39,860 --> 00:01:40,990
Most likely.

23
00:01:40,990 --> 00:01:44,580
But I'm sure she left no evidence.

24
00:01:45,120 --> 00:01:46,000
You're right.

25
00:01:46,370 --> 00:01:51,210
Ah, well. Our job is to take over this fort...

26
00:01:51,210 --> 00:01:56,300
...while that fox is being investigated in Central by a herd of tigers.

27
00:02:04,140 --> 00:02:06,390
Oh, if it isn't the Major General.

28
00:02:07,480 --> 00:02:09,810
I still can't believe you were transferred to Central.

29
00:02:09,810 --> 00:02:11,190
What connections did you use?

30
00:02:11,480 --> 00:02:13,820
I believe it's simply an honest display of my capabilities.

31
00:02:14,570 --> 00:02:16,400
Says the fresh meat.

32
00:02:19,490 --> 00:02:21,820
What brings you here today?

33
00:02:22,200 --> 00:02:24,370
I've been summoned by the Führer President.

34
00:02:24,370 --> 00:02:26,740
I may not be able to return to Briggs for a while.

35
00:02:28,080 --> 00:02:29,290
"For a while"?

36
00:02:29,710 --> 00:02:32,500
Then I'm going to have to take you to dinner at least once.

37
00:02:32,500 --> 00:02:33,630
Is it your treat?

38
00:02:34,340 --> 00:02:37,170
If you'll let me eat until you go bankrupt, I don't mind going for dinner.

39
00:02:37,590 --> 00:02:39,630
I guess I'll give up on the meal, then...

40
00:02:39,630 --> 00:02:42,970
Both your wallet and your balls are pea-sized, I see.

41
00:02:43,640 --> 00:02:46,180
How about some flowers instead?

42
00:02:48,140 --> 00:02:51,100
There are many great florists in Central, after all.

43
00:02:51,850 --> 00:02:52,650
I see.

44
00:02:57,860 --> 00:02:59,150
You may enter.

45
00:02:59,150 --> 00:03:00,150
Yes, sir.

46
00:03:09,830 --> 00:03:13,170
Now, Major General Armstrong...

47
00:03:13,170 --> 00:03:17,550
...let me hear more about
Lieutenant General Raven's disappearance.

48
00:03:18,300 --> 00:03:19,800
What did you do?

49
00:03:20,420 --> 00:03:22,470
I won't be able to hide this.

50
00:03:23,430 --> 00:03:29,810
Why would a man as great as you choose to place a fool like Raven by his side?

51
00:03:31,770 --> 00:03:34,440
So you got rid of him?

52
00:03:34,440 --> 00:03:36,150
You don't need him.

53
00:03:36,610 --> 00:03:40,360
Having a subordinate with such a loose tongue would do you no good.

54
00:03:41,320 --> 00:03:44,570
What did Lieutenant General Raven tell you?

55
00:03:44,570 --> 00:03:46,450
Something about an immortal army...

56
00:03:46,450 --> 00:03:49,910
...the history of this country, and your real identity.

57
00:03:50,580 --> 00:03:53,830
He told me many things I didn't even ask for.

58
00:03:55,540 --> 00:04:00,090
So you still chose to respond to
my summons after hearing all that?

59
00:04:00,090 --> 00:04:04,300
Yes, to request the seat the idiot had been placing his ass on.

60
00:04:06,800 --> 00:04:10,060
Interesting, as expected of you.

61
00:04:11,350 --> 00:04:14,690
Very well. You may have the position.

62
00:04:14,690 --> 00:04:19,690
In exchange, I'll have one of my men govern over Briggs. Are you fine with this?

63
00:04:20,230 --> 00:04:21,900
As you wish, sir.

64
00:04:22,400 --> 00:04:25,450
They are powerful soldiers I trained with great care.

65
00:04:25,450 --> 00:04:28,070
I'm sure you'll like them.

66
00:04:28,780 --> 00:04:33,830
Interesting. Do your best, human.

67
00:04:39,090 --> 00:04:41,670
"Nothing ventured, nothing gained."

68
00:04:42,090 --> 00:04:44,970
So the Major General ventured into the enemy's lair by her own will.

69
00:04:45,380 --> 00:04:48,470
Yeah. This place also belongs to them now.

70
00:04:48,470 --> 00:04:51,100
But they're unaware...

71
00:04:51,470 --> 00:05:00,940
...Briggs is a giant monolith that can act with a united will, even if its master happens to be away.

72
00:05:01,820 --> 00:05:05,740
From here on, it's a war between bears and tigers.

73
00:05:06,260 --> 00:05:09,260
Homunculus
(The Dwarf in the Flask)

74
00:05:06,260 --> 00:05:09,260
Homunculus
(The Dwarf in the Flask)

75
00:05:13,540 --> 00:05:15,540
Is that seat free?

76
00:05:17,830 --> 00:05:18,670
Yes.

77
00:05:21,590 --> 00:05:23,250
How's your work progressing?

78
00:05:23,250 --> 00:05:24,800
As you can see,

79
00:05:25,720 --> 00:05:28,630
I can't finish everything unless I multitask during my meals, as well.

80
00:05:29,800 --> 00:05:30,800
And you?

81
00:05:31,350 --> 00:05:34,560
There's so much to memorize; I'm fairly busy.

82
00:05:35,100 --> 00:05:38,190
But the Führer President does his job very quickly, so I do not have to worry about that.

83
00:05:38,190 --> 00:05:39,690
He doesn't loaf either, unlike a certain someone.

84
00:05:41,060 --> 00:05:43,360
I have a feeling this topic is heading in a direction I don't like.

85
00:05:50,240 --> 00:05:51,370
That reminds me...

86
00:05:54,910 --> 00:05:57,000
Scar is apparently up north.

87
00:05:58,410 --> 00:06:00,290
So are the Elric brothers.

88
00:06:02,040 --> 00:06:03,210
I see.

89
00:06:05,130 --> 00:06:08,300
My old classmates, Lucy and Ian, are also up north.

90
00:06:08,300 --> 00:06:09,930
They tell me many things.

91
00:06:11,640 --> 00:06:15,060
If I recall, the north and the east will be holding joint exercises in the spring.

92
00:06:15,060 --> 00:06:20,690
Yes, we've been defeated countless times by Major Miles and Captain Buccaneer.

93
00:06:21,270 --> 00:06:23,770
Miles... Buccaneer...

94
00:06:24,320 --> 00:06:28,570
York, Ida, and Sugar, too.

95
00:06:30,030 --> 00:06:36,700
Havoc, Oscar, Mike, Uni, Nora, Charley...

96
00:06:36,700 --> 00:06:39,080
Uni again, then Lucy...

97
00:06:41,000 --> 00:06:44,000
Uni comes again, then next... is Sterling!

98
00:06:45,840 --> 00:06:49,010
"Selim Bradley is Homunculus".

99
00:06:53,550 --> 00:06:56,720
I guess there's no way that can't  be true.

100
00:06:59,600 --> 00:07:03,400
Just what is about to happen here in Central?

101
00:07:14,160 --> 00:07:15,280
Boy.

102
00:07:17,700 --> 00:07:19,500
Hey, you over there.

103
00:07:20,080 --> 00:07:21,210
Oh, crap!

104
00:07:21,210 --> 00:07:22,710
Don't worry.

105
00:07:24,500 --> 00:07:25,840
Over here.

106
00:07:28,630 --> 00:07:29,670
What the hell?

107
00:07:29,670 --> 00:07:31,130
Come on.

108
00:07:31,130 --> 00:07:35,590
Aren't you at least a little surprised?

109
00:07:35,590 --> 00:07:38,060
If I do get surprised, will you give me something?

110
00:07:38,060 --> 00:07:41,560
I guess you're always at ease. I like you.

111
00:07:41,560 --> 00:07:43,600
What's your name?

112
00:07:43,980 --> 00:07:45,400
Slave Number 23.

113
00:07:45,400 --> 00:07:49,400
I didn't ask for a number. I want your real name.

114
00:07:49,690 --> 00:07:51,820
I don't have a name. I'm a slave.

115
00:07:51,820 --> 00:07:53,030
Slave?

116
00:07:53,030 --> 00:07:59,080
People who are stripped of their rights and freedom, and are exchanged as possessions in conveyance?

117
00:07:59,080 --> 00:08:00,200
Conveyance?

118
00:08:00,200 --> 00:08:04,250
To transfer property and rights and such.

119
00:08:05,670 --> 00:08:08,250
You're not very bright, are you?

120
00:08:08,250 --> 00:08:09,590
Shut up!

121
00:08:09,590 --> 00:08:14,300
I don't understand how I was born from someone like you.

122
00:08:15,380 --> 00:08:18,220
You're the one who gave me blood, aren't you?

123
00:08:20,890 --> 00:08:24,060
They did take a lot of blood from me to use for experiments...

124
00:08:24,480 --> 00:08:28,770
I was born because you gave me blood.

125
00:08:29,730 --> 00:08:32,860
Thank you. Umm...

126
00:08:33,240 --> 00:08:36,320
"Slave Number 23" just sounds too cold.

127
00:08:36,320 --> 00:08:38,660
I'll give you a name, then.

128
00:08:38,660 --> 00:08:40,530
Who the hell do you think you are?

129
00:08:40,530 --> 00:08:44,410
Don't you want a cool name? Let's see...

130
00:08:44,410 --> 00:08:48,880
Teo... Teofrastus Bombastus.

131
00:08:47,880 --> 00:08:48,880
Too long.

132
00:08:50,040 --> 00:08:55,260
Ah, it can't be too long; else you won't be able to memorize it. You're dumb, after all.

133
00:08:55,260 --> 00:08:56,470
Quit saying that!

134
00:08:57,180 --> 00:08:58,760
Then how about Van?

135
00:08:58,760 --> 00:09:01,810
Van Hohenheim.

136
00:09:02,140 --> 00:09:03,770
Van Hohen, eh?

137
00:09:04,230 --> 00:09:06,560
I should be able to remember that.

138
00:09:06,560 --> 00:09:08,190
You spell it like...

139
00:09:08,190 --> 00:09:10,940
Wait, do you know how to read and write?

140
00:09:10,940 --> 00:09:13,780
I don't need to know to work.

141
00:09:13,780 --> 00:09:15,610
The work of a slave, right?

142
00:09:17,910 --> 00:09:20,370
Don't you want freedom and rights?

143
00:09:20,370 --> 00:09:26,250
Do you plan on ending your life as a slave without gaining basic human rights?

144
00:09:27,790 --> 00:09:32,170
That's the same as being in this stuffy flask.

145
00:09:34,000 --> 00:09:37,380
I'm going to share my knowledge with you, Van Hohenheim.

146
00:09:39,680 --> 00:09:44,310
Hey... What are  you?

147
00:09:45,220 --> 00:09:46,560
What should I call you?

148
00:09:47,060 --> 00:09:52,730
The Little One Inside the Flask. So... call me "Homunculus".

149
00:10:05,740 --> 00:10:10,210
All was created from one, and it eventually returns to one.

150
00:10:11,290 --> 00:10:13,710
In other words, one is all.

151
00:10:13,710 --> 00:10:16,380
All exists due to one...

152
00:10:16,380 --> 00:10:18,800
...and all exists within one.

153
00:10:18,800 --> 00:10:22,470
If one does not contain all, then there exists nothing.

154
00:10:24,100 --> 00:10:25,140
You pass.

155
00:10:25,890 --> 00:10:29,730
You're now a fine alchemist, Hohenheim.

156
00:10:30,940 --> 00:10:33,060
I'm still not good enough to be on my own.

157
00:10:33,560 --> 00:10:36,570
My abilities are far beneath yours, Master.

158
00:10:39,860 --> 00:10:41,320
You know, I'm really thankful.

159
00:10:41,320 --> 00:10:42,740
For what?

160
00:10:42,740 --> 00:10:46,950
Because you gave me knowledge,
I'm able to live a good life like this.

161
00:10:47,410 --> 00:10:49,620
I'm also happy to be in Master's favor.

162
00:10:50,330 --> 00:10:54,630
It may be possible that I can marry someone in the future and start my own family.

163
00:10:54,920 --> 00:10:56,960
A family, eh?

164
00:10:56,960 --> 00:10:59,210
Humans are inconvenient creatures, aren't they?

165
00:10:59,210 --> 00:11:03,970
The species can't live on unless they all create a community and expand.

166
00:11:03,970 --> 00:11:05,850
Don't talk like that.

167
00:11:06,260 --> 00:11:11,480
It may be stupid in your eyes,
but having friends and family...

168
00:11:11,940 --> 00:11:15,190
...may bring one happiness.

169
00:11:15,480 --> 00:11:16,900
For us humans, that is.

170
00:11:16,900 --> 00:11:18,690
Really?

171
00:11:18,690 --> 00:11:21,240
Then what do you consider happiness?

172
00:11:21,950 --> 00:11:23,200
Let's see...

173
00:11:23,780 --> 00:11:29,950
I don't want to be too greedy, but I guess being able to leave this flask would make me happy.

174
00:11:39,300 --> 00:11:41,010
Immortality...

175
00:11:41,470 --> 00:11:46,680
I wonder why fools who gained ultimate authority and prosperity begin to wish for that.

176
00:11:46,680 --> 00:11:48,010
Mind your tongue!

177
00:11:48,010 --> 00:11:49,720
You're talking to the King!

178
00:11:50,520 --> 00:11:53,730
If you continue to be disrespectful, I'll break the flask!

179
00:11:53,730 --> 00:11:57,610
You're going to destroy the source of the knowledge you don't know about?

180
00:11:58,730 --> 00:12:00,610
Cease your prattling.

181
00:12:01,320 --> 00:12:04,610
Can you make me immortal or not?

182
00:12:04,610 --> 00:12:06,990
Growing impatient as you age, huh?

183
00:12:06,990 --> 00:12:10,160
How sad, King of Xerxes.

184
00:12:12,910 --> 00:12:17,040
Fine, I'll tell you how to achieve immortality.

185
00:12:20,920 --> 00:12:22,920
What's with the construction?

186
00:12:22,920 --> 00:12:24,800
We're making a waterway for irrigation.

187
00:12:24,800 --> 00:12:28,600
The King ordered a waterway to extend around the entire country.

188
00:12:28,600 --> 00:12:31,060
Nothing less to be expected from the King of Xerxes.

189
00:12:31,060 --> 00:12:34,640
He even thinks about commoners like us.

190
00:12:34,640 --> 00:12:35,890
That's right.

191
00:12:42,150 --> 00:12:44,740
Kill them all. Understood?

192
00:12:44,740 --> 00:12:45,650
Yes, sir!

193
00:12:57,830 --> 00:13:00,630
Hurry! Waste no time!

194
00:13:01,460 --> 00:13:04,340
Hurry and carve a bloody crest into the land!

195
00:13:10,220 --> 00:13:12,100
The village to the north was raided?

196
00:13:12,100 --> 00:13:13,680
I heard everyone there was killed.

197
00:13:13,680 --> 00:13:15,310
And the same thing happened in the village to the west last time.

198
00:13:15,310 --> 00:13:16,940
I wonder who's behind it...

199
00:13:17,440 --> 00:13:19,060
How terrible.

200
00:13:19,060 --> 00:13:20,980
Yeah, how awful.

201
00:13:41,380 --> 00:13:45,960
Your Majesty, the transmutation circle is finally complete.

202
00:13:47,930 --> 00:13:51,220
Truly, it has been a long time.

203
00:13:53,310 --> 00:13:55,770
This is all we need to do, right?

204
00:13:56,060 --> 00:13:58,850
Yeah, you'll be able to become immortal.

205
00:14:17,500 --> 00:14:18,870
That's amazing.

206
00:14:19,710 --> 00:14:21,880
The King is going to become immortal.

207
00:14:26,260 --> 00:14:29,090
I guess it's what they call the turning point of the century.

208
00:14:45,690 --> 00:14:48,190
So this is immortality...

209
00:14:53,280 --> 00:14:54,740
What's this?!

210
00:14:56,830 --> 00:15:01,040
You said that since we're in the center of it, we wouldn't be harmed!

211
00:15:06,800 --> 00:15:07,630
What?

212
00:15:08,460 --> 00:15:09,840
What's happening?!

213
00:15:09,840 --> 00:15:11,630
Hey! Homunculus!

214
00:15:13,300 --> 00:15:18,430
The true center of the transmutation circle is where you're standing right now.

215
00:15:18,430 --> 00:15:19,270
What?!

216
00:15:19,730 --> 00:15:24,560
I opened the gate using your blood inside of me.

217
00:15:25,190 --> 00:15:28,320
You're a relative that shares my blood, Hohenheim!

218
00:15:28,980 --> 00:15:32,990
Right now, you and I are at the center of the world!

219
00:16:45,390 --> 00:16:46,190
Your Majesty!

220
00:16:52,780 --> 00:16:53,900
Master!

221
00:16:56,910 --> 00:16:58,120
He's dead.

222
00:17:05,960 --> 00:17:08,170
Is anyone here?!

223
00:17:09,920 --> 00:17:11,170
Willard!

224
00:17:12,000 --> 00:17:13,090
Mechthild!

225
00:17:13,840 --> 00:17:14,920
Linemile!

226
00:17:15,630 --> 00:17:16,510
Tony!

227
00:17:17,010 --> 00:17:18,340
Meiyou!

228
00:17:29,560 --> 00:17:33,030
Please... Someone, say something.

229
00:17:34,190 --> 00:17:37,610
It's no use. Everyone has had their souls taken from them.

230
00:17:39,570 --> 00:17:41,070
Your Majesty!

231
00:17:42,490 --> 00:17:44,040
You were all right...

232
00:17:44,040 --> 00:17:45,040
So...

233
00:17:47,580 --> 00:17:51,000
...How do you like your new body?

234
00:17:51,000 --> 00:17:53,460
It's... me...

235
00:17:53,460 --> 00:17:58,340
I created a body for myself using
the information stored in your blood.

236
00:18:00,010 --> 00:18:04,220
Finally, I can walk with my own two feet.

237
00:18:05,680 --> 00:18:09,270
You're... Homunculus?

238
00:18:09,900 --> 00:18:11,900
What is this?! What did you do?!

239
00:18:11,900 --> 00:18:16,900
In return for you giving me blood, I gave you a name and shared my knowledge with you.

240
00:18:16,900 --> 00:18:21,160
I also gave you an eternal body.

241
00:18:22,320 --> 00:18:23,830
Eternal?

242
00:18:23,830 --> 00:18:27,250
Try focusing all of your consciousness into yourself.

243
00:18:32,130 --> 00:18:33,790
Can't you hear the voices?

244
00:18:33,790 --> 00:18:40,630
The voices of all the people, who lived in this country, sacrificed for your immortal body.

245
00:18:41,260 --> 00:18:44,890
Well, half of them went to me.

246
00:18:46,770 --> 00:18:49,890
Thanks for your help, Hohenheim.

247
00:19:01,700 --> 00:19:02,990
Mr. Hohenheim?

248
00:19:04,660 --> 00:19:05,780
It really is  you!

249
00:19:12,170 --> 00:19:16,000
Wow, I didn't know you were Ed and Al's father.

250
00:19:16,000 --> 00:19:19,170
I didn't expect you to be the master of my sons, either...

251
00:19:20,300 --> 00:19:22,470
I hear you did a lot for them.

252
00:19:22,470 --> 00:19:24,550
No, not at all.

253
00:19:25,680 --> 00:19:26,430
Miss Izumi?

254
00:19:26,430 --> 00:19:28,600
Are you all right, Izumi?!

255
00:19:29,310 --> 00:19:31,020
I'll get your medicine...

256
00:19:31,020 --> 00:19:32,390
Let me take a look at her.

257
00:19:33,140 --> 00:19:35,730
I know a thing or two about medicine.

258
00:19:41,990 --> 00:19:44,570
Don't worry, this isn't anything new.

259
00:19:45,490 --> 00:19:46,950
This is certainly something to worry about.

260
00:19:47,280 --> 00:19:49,950
Mr. Sig, please get a cab.

261
00:19:50,870 --> 00:19:51,750
Hurry!

262
00:19:51,750 --> 00:19:53,460
R-Right!

263
00:19:57,920 --> 00:19:58,960
Miss Izumi...

264
00:20:00,630 --> 00:20:03,300
You saw the truth, didn't you?

265
00:20:04,300 --> 00:20:06,050
What did you sacrifice?

266
00:20:08,180 --> 00:20:09,680
Please don't try to hide it.

267
00:20:14,480 --> 00:20:16,940
They took a few of my organs.

268
00:20:17,860 --> 00:20:20,400
I tried to revive my dead baby.

269
00:20:22,400 --> 00:20:23,950
I see.

270
00:20:26,870 --> 00:20:28,450
I see...

271
00:20:30,540 --> 00:20:31,910
If you'll excuse me.

272
00:20:50,310 --> 00:20:52,140
Izumi! Hang in there!

273
00:20:52,140 --> 00:20:53,390
Izumi!

274
00:20:53,730 --> 00:20:56,350
Calm down, Dear. I'm fine.

275
00:20:56,690 --> 00:20:58,150
You were stabbed in the stomach!

276
00:20:58,810 --> 00:21:01,480
But I can breathe more easily now.

277
00:21:02,150 --> 00:21:03,150
Show me your wound.

278
00:21:04,690 --> 00:21:06,200
There's no wound.

279
00:21:06,660 --> 00:21:08,740
That can't be!

280
00:21:11,080 --> 00:21:16,080
The organs that were taken are the proof of your sins, so I can't bring them back.

281
00:21:16,080 --> 00:21:20,170
But I rearranged your insides a bit to ease the flow of blood.

282
00:21:20,170 --> 00:21:24,550
Miss Izumi, you can't die just yet.

283
00:21:26,630 --> 00:21:27,840
Hohenheim...

284
00:21:28,640 --> 00:21:31,300
Just... what exactly are  you?

285
00:21:33,060 --> 00:21:38,980
I'm a human by the name of Van Hohenheim...

286
00:21:40,360 --> 00:21:42,020
A philosopher's stone in human form.

287
00:21:56,250 --> 00:22:01,210
The promise we never made

288
00:21:56,250 --> 00:22:01,210
Kawashita hazu no nai yakasoku ga

289
00:22:01,210 --> 00:22:02,000
yet again

290
00:22:01,210 --> 00:22:02,000
Kyou mo

291
00:22:02,000 --> 00:22:06,840
tries to snatch our future away from us.

292
00:22:02,000 --> 00:22:06,840
Bokura no mirai wo ubaou to suru

293
00:22:08,470 --> 00:22:12,430
Why is it that we can't rejoice

294
00:22:08,470 --> 00:22:12,430
Hoshigatteita mono wo te ni shitemo

295
00:22:12,430 --> 00:22:13,430
straight from the heart

296
00:22:12,430 --> 00:22:13,430
Sunao ni

297
00:22:13,430 --> 00:22:18,390
when we obtain something we've always been after?

298
00:22:13,430 --> 00:22:18,390
Umaku waraenai nowa nazedarou

299
00:22:19,060 --> 00:22:24,110
The overflowing tears aren't from feebleness or remorse.

300
00:22:19,060 --> 00:22:24,110
Afureru namida wo yowasa ya koukai ja nai

301
00:22:24,770 --> 00:22:28,900
They're fragments born from agony.

302
00:22:24,770 --> 00:22:28,900
Itami ga unda kakera de

303
00:22:30,570 --> 00:22:33,950
Of all the moments and destinies,

304
00:22:30,570 --> 00:22:33,950
Donna shunkan datte unmei datte

305
00:22:33,950 --> 00:22:42,710
I realized there's one absolute certainty.

306
00:22:33,950 --> 00:22:42,710
Hitotsu dake tashika na mono ga aru to shitta

307
00:22:42,710 --> 00:22:45,250
Even if things get tough and I'm at my limit

308
00:22:42,710 --> 00:22:45,250
Genkai datte konnan datte

309
00:22:45,250 --> 00:22:49,260
I refuse to give up.

310
00:22:45,250 --> 00:22:49,260
Akirametakunaiyo

311
00:22:49,260 --> 00:22:54,140
Please, don't let go.

312
00:22:49,260 --> 00:22:54,140
Konomama hanasanaide

313
00:22:54,140 --> 00:23:01,980
I can feel the warmth of your right hand

314
00:22:54,140 --> 00:23:01,980
Kataku nigirishimeta kimi no migite no nukumori

315
00:23:01,980 --> 00:23:05,650
where it's tightly joined with my left.

316
00:23:01,980 --> 00:23:05,650
Koko ni arukara

317
00:23:13,490 --> 00:23:17,450
The Philosopher's Stone,
the Heavenly Stone, the Great Elixir.

318
00:23:17,950 --> 00:23:20,460
Just like how the philosopher's stone has many names,

319
00:23:20,460 --> 00:23:22,750
its form isn't always that of a stone.

320
00:23:24,210 --> 00:23:27,170
The one Doctor Marcoh had was almost like a gel.

321
00:23:28,130 --> 00:23:32,260
Kimblee's looked like a crystal, and it was about this big.

322
00:23:32,260 --> 00:23:36,760
Since it possesses so much energy, I pictured something far larger...

323
00:23:36,760 --> 00:23:40,560
I've never seen one bigger than a pebble.

324
00:23:41,480 --> 00:23:47,940
If it's something even larger, that would mean an enormous number of humans was used to create it.

325
00:23:48,860 --> 00:23:52,240
I'd rather not see one.

326
00:23:59,990 --> 00:24:04,250
If one wishes to gain something,
one must present something of equal value.

327
00:24:05,170 --> 00:24:08,170
That is the principle behind alchemy.

328
00:24:08,170 --> 00:24:11,130
It is also the principle behind everything else.

329
00:24:12,220 --> 00:24:16,820
Next time, Fullmetal Alchemist:

330
00:24:16,820 --> 00:24:20,320
The Abyss

331
00:24:16,820 --> 00:24:20,320
Episode 41, The Abyss.

332
00:24:21,100 --> 00:24:26,480
His softness seeks pain from the boy as an equal exchange.
